To obtain OPLS-AA torsion parameters for specific missing cases:

As an example, we wanted parameters to treat 2-chloro-N-methylacetamide. The Z-matrix was 
derived from nma.z in the aazmat directory by modifying the CH3 group to CH2Cl using standard 
OPLS-AA atom types for alkyl chlorides. An optimization was run and BOSS noted that torsion 
parameters for Cl-CT-C-O and Cl-CT-C-N were missing and that it was using the nearest 
matches instead, CT-CT-C-O and CT-CT-C-N. Dihedral driving was then executed as in the 
dihdrive test job and it was found that the profile is 1-fold with Cl-C-C-O cis being 5.5 kcal/mol 
higher in energy than trans. With Gaussian98, a 6-31G* torsion profile was run and the barrier 
was found to be 1-fold with height 4.1 kcal/mol. To obtain this result, entries were made in 
oplsaa.par for Cl-CT-C-O and Cl-CT-C-N with all Vs = 0. The dihedral driving was rerun and the 
barrier remained at 5.5 kcal/mol. The barrier was reduced to 4.1 kcal/mol by modifying the V1
terms in oplsaa.par:
       V1        V2         V3       V4
352  -0.650     0.000     0.000     0.0        Cl-CT-C -O      2-chloroamide wlj fit to 6-31G*
353   0.650     0.000     0.000     0.0        Cl-CT-C -N      2-chloroamide wlj fit to 6-31G*

More generally, I would record the ab initio energy profile in a database program like JMP,
and one should also consider using higher-level ab initio calculations such as LMP2/cc-pVTZ(-f).
Instead of JMP, one could use our own xlfit or QikFit in a similar manner entering the data in a CSV.
Then you need to compute the OPLS-AA profile with the to-be-determined torsion parameters
with all Vs set to zero. Subtract the two columns and the residual is what needs to be fitted
with the Fourier series. Add columns with 1 + cos phi, 1 - cos 2phi, and 1 + cos 3phi.
Then run the regression analysis with JMP to determine the optimal V1, V2, and V3. The need for 
V4 terms is rare, but they can be handled analogously, if needed. If any Vs are near zero (+/- 0.1 
kcal/mol), set them to zero (exclude them from the fit) and refit again for the final Vs.

